# 09b round-6 distinguishing ablations of clean payload C6

Payload C6: b3d0d59f18f6c2b1d0a49746428123d84dd80df2.
Each ablation changes exactly one behaviour in a detached worktree at C6, runs
packages/kernel/tests/*.test.ts against it, and is reverted before the next.
An ablation is REJECTED when named packet cases fail; that is what makes those cases
distinguishing rather than merely green.

Two ablations are new for the two reopened P1s. N1 removes the restored serializer
environment while keeping the safe clone: the ambient-prototype cases from round 5 still
pass (the clone still neutralizes them), but the new capture-time `Object.keys` /
`Array.prototype.join` cases fail — proving the new failure is the execution environment,
not the clone (contrast P6, which removes the clone while keeping the environment: the
round-5 `toJSON` cases fail there instead). N3 restores multiple `options.bound` reads.

